### Page 1 of 1

```text
RESOLUTION NO.  _________

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION PROVIDING FOR THE CITY OF CHEYENNE TO
APPLY FOR “CARES ACT” AND OTHER FEDERALLY AVAILABLE
FUNDS TO ADDRESS THE COVID-19 PANDEMIC

WHEREAS, the Coronavirus Aid, Relief and Economic Security Act (CARES Act),P.L.
116-136 was passed by Congress, signed by the President, and published in the Federal Register
on March 27, 2020; and

WHEREAS, the Wyoming Legislature enacted and the Governor of the State of
Wyoming signed into law 2020 SEA 1/SF 1001, effective May 20, 2020, authorizing the State
Loan and Investment Board to administer distribution of CARES Act and other federally
provided funds to address the COVID-19 pandemic; and

WHEREAS, the Wyoming Office of State Lands, on behalf of the Wyoming State Loan
and Investment Board, has been designated to receive, review and approve CARES Act grant
applications from Wyoming municipalities; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne is unable to provide critical and essential services to
its citizens without obtaining CARES Act and other available federal funds to address the
COVID-19 pandemic.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, that the City of Cheyenne through the Office of the Mayor and with the
concurrence of the City Attorney may, and should, apply for CARES Act and other available
federal funds to address the COVID-19 pandemic and do so without further action of the
Governing Body.

PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED this ______ day of __________________,
2020.

__________________________________________

Marian J. Orr, Mayor

(SEAL)

ATTEST:

____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
```
